@Editor Help
The editor menus can be operated by using the arrows up/down and the
page up and page down keys, or using tab; push enter to activate the
selected menu item. Some letters are highlighted in green; you can
push ALT and the highlighted to select it. Some items allow entering
numbers or text; you can push CTRL+U to erase the number/text.

You can push ALT+? on almost any screen to display context-sensitive
online help for that screen.

Remember to save before you quit; otherwise your changes are lost.

The main screen of the editor contains the following submenus:
!-blist;Board list
!-slist;Screen list
!-stvar;Status variables
!-element;Elements
!-appmap;Appearance mapping
!-anima;Animations
!-numform;Numeric formats
!-edithelp;Help lumps
!global;Global script
!more;More

:global
The global script can be shared by any board that does not have the
"suppress global scripts" flag.

:more
The "More" submenu contains:

þ Auto pause: If selected, then the game is automatically paused when it
starts (you can still push the pause key to toggle it, whether or not this
is selected). While it is paused, a turn is only advanced when a key is
pushed, and otherwise does nothing.

